// correlation_loss.ivl -- interval domain loses relational information.
// x is any integer, y is assigned from x, so x and y are always equal.
// The expression (x - y) is therefore always exactly 0, but independent
// intervals only know x in Top and y in Top, hence the analyzer reports a
// *possible* division by zero.  This is a true (unavoidable) false alarm of
// the non-relational domain; exhaustive execution confirms zero real crash.
input var x;
var y = x;
var z = 1 / (x - y);
